windows: the processor count Wine reports, and FineWine's names for Wine's exports

Two small things in the Windows front ends.

The processor count. When Wine asks for the emulated processor's description, FEX replaced
the count Wine had filled in with the count from its own CPUID leaf 1 plus one. That CPUID
field already holds the count, so x64 and 32-bit programs were told of one processor more
than there is: 9 on an 8-core Mac, 11 on a 10-core one (seen in a game launcher's own report).
A program that pins a thread to the last processor it was told of asked for one that does not
exist. The count Wine filled in is now kept, which also makes it follow WINE_CPU_TOPOLOGY
(Wine runtime patch 0058).

The names. FEX asks ntdll for wine_get_version to know it is on Wine, and (patch 0014) for
wine_get_host_version to know the host's page size. A FineWine prefix can hide those names
from programs (FINEWINE_HIDE_WINE_EXPORTS, runtime patch 0058); FEX would then take the host
for Windows and its pages for 4K, which brings back the bug 0014 fixed. It now asks for
__finewine_get_version and __finewine_get_host_version first, which are never hidden.

Checked with tests/runtime/compat-switches.c (the count) and code-rewrite-silent.c with the
names hidden.

Local patch only: FEX does not take AI-written code.

diff --git a/Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp b/Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp
--- a/Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp
@@ -186,7 +186,13 @@
 }
 
 void CPUFeatures::UpdateInformation(SYSTEM_CPU_INFORMATION* Info) {
-  Info->MaximumProcessors = CpuInfo.MaximumProcessors;
+  // FineWine: the count Wine filled in is kept. FEX replaced it with the count from its own CPUID
+  // leaf 1 plus one, but that field already holds the count, so x64 and 32-bit programs were told
+  // of one processor more than there is (9 on an 8-core Mac), and of every processor when Wine had
+  // been asked to report fewer (WINE_CPU_TOPOLOGY).
+  if (!Info->MaximumProcessors) {
+    Info->MaximumProcessors = CpuInfo.MaximumProcessors > 1 ? CpuInfo.MaximumProcessors - 1 : 1;
+  }
   Info->ProcessorArchitecture = CpuInfo.ProcessorArchitecture;
   Info->ProcessorLevel = CpuInfo.ProcessorLevel;
   Info->ProcessorRevision = CpuInfo.ProcessorRevision;
diff --git a/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp b/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
--- a/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
@@ -28,7 +28,13 @@
   // sets it by hand (4096 is how it was before), to rule this in or out when something misbehaves.
   TrapGranule = FEXCore::Utils::FEX_PAGE_SIZE;
   using HostVersionFn = void(__cdecl*)(const char**, const char**);
-  if (const auto HostVersion = reinterpret_cast<HostVersionFn>(GetProcAddress(GetModuleHandleW(L"ntdll.dll"), "wine_get_host_version"))) {
+  // The first name is one FineWine's Wine keeps when a prefix hides Wine's own exports from programs.
+  const auto NtDllModule = GetModuleHandleW(L"ntdll.dll");
+  auto HostVersion = reinterpret_cast<HostVersionFn>(GetProcAddress(NtDllModule, "__finewine_get_host_version"));
+  if (!HostVersion) {
+    HostVersion = reinterpret_cast<HostVersionFn>(GetProcAddress(NtDllModule, "wine_get_host_version"));
+  }
+  if (HostVersion) {
     const char* SysName = nullptr;
     const char* Release = nullptr;
     HostVersion(&SysName, &Release);
diff --git a/Source/Windows/WOW64/Module.cpp b/Source/Windows/WOW64/Module.cpp
--- a/Source/Windows/WOW64/Module.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/WOW64/Module.cpp
@@ -582,7 +582,8 @@
   SignalDelegator = fextl::make_unique<FEX::DummyHandlers::DummySignalDelegator>();
   SyscallHandler = fextl::make_unique<WowSyscallHandler>();
   const auto NtDll = GetModuleHandleW(L"ntdll.dll");
-  const bool IsWine = !!GetProcAddress(NtDll, "wine_get_version");
+  // FineWine: the first name stays when a prefix hides Wine's own exports from programs.
+  const bool IsWine = GetProcAddress(NtDll, "__finewine_get_version") || GetProcAddress(NtDll, "wine_get_version");
   OvercommitTracker.emplace(IsWine);
 
   FEX::Windows::Allocator::SetupHooks(NtDll);
diff --git a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
--- a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
@@ -774,7 +774,8 @@
   SyscallHandler = fextl::make_unique<Exception::ECSyscallHandler>();
 
   const auto NtDll = GetModuleHandleW(L"ntdll.dll");
-  const bool IsWine = !!GetProcAddress(NtDll, "wine_get_version");
+  // FineWine: the first name stays when a prefix hides Wine's own exports from programs.
+  const bool IsWine = GetProcAddress(NtDll, "__finewine_get_version") || GetProcAddress(NtDll, "wine_get_version");
   // FineWine: FEX_EAGERCOMMIT=1 turns off committing emulator memory a piece at a time (the
